            <ArticleTitle>Benevolent Renal Angiomyolipoma with Intra-cardiac Extension-A Challenge in Diagnosis and Management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-261</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12262-016-1553-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While intra-caval and intra-cardiac extension of retroperitoneal tumors is extremely rare, it is almost unheard-of in benign tumors. We report the challenges in diagnosis and management of the first case of a renal angiomyolipoma (AML) with intra-ventricular extension in a young man who presented with pain and a lump in the abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
